    "scenarioText": "Prakriti Limited is a listed company engaged in the manufacture of eco -friendly \nhome appliances. During the financial year, the company significantly expanded \nits operations by setting up a new manufacturing facility in a semi -rural \nlocation. The expansion was aimed at increasing production capacity while \nbenefiting from lower operational costs and proximity to raw material suppliers. \nDuring the statutory audit of Prakriti Limited, the auditor became aware of the \nundisclosed environmental violations and labour -related non -compliances. \nManagement represented that the issues were operational in nature and \nassured corrective action. Relying on management representations, the auditor \ndid not include any specific reference to these matters in the audit report. \nThe company sources raw materials from a diverse supplier base and employs \na large workforce, a substantial portion of which consists of contractual labour \nengaged through third -party contractors. Prakriti Limited sells its products \nthrough online platforms as well as a widespread network of distributors across \nIndia. \nBeing a listed entity, Prakriti Limited is required to comply with the Business \nResponsibility and Sustainability Reporting (BRSR) framework. During the year, \nthe following issues came to the attention of stakeholders and regulators: \n• Prakriti Limited has published its sustainability policies and environmental \ncommitments on its official website. However, certain material environmental \nviolations relating to emissions and waste management at the newly established \nplant were disclosed to the public only after these violations were highlighted \nin media reports. The company did not make timely or voluntary disclosures to \nits stakeholders when the violations first occurred. \n• Contractual workers employed at the new manufacturing facility raised \ncomplaints regarding delayed payment of wages by contractors and \nabsence of adequate safety measures at the workplace. The workers \nalleged that despite being aware of these issues, the c ompany did not \ntake sufficient steps to ensure compliance by contractors. \n\n• Prakriti Limited collects customer data through its online sales platform \nfor order processing and customer engagement. During the year, it was \nobserved that the company shared customer data with third -party \nmarketing agencies without obtaining explicit consent from custo mers. \nStatutory auditor CA. Manik, during the statutory audit of Prakriti Limited , \nbecame aware of the undisclosed environmental violations and labour-related \nnon-compliances . Management represented that the issues were operational in \nnature and assured corrective action. Relying on management representations, \nthe auditor did not include any specific reference to these matters in the audit \nreport. \nBased on the above facts, answer the following:",
