    "scenarioText": "M/s BAT & Co., a firm of Chartered Accountants, recently launched its official \nwebsite “ bat-ca.com”. The website featured bright neon colours, details of the \npartners, and listed some major clients with the fees charged. The website also \nused a “push” technology, where updates were automatically sent to \nsubscribers without them requesting it. \nAround the same time, Mr. P, a partner in the firm, appeared on a business \nchannel TV interview and handed over a bio -data of the firm to the interviewer. \nThe bio-data contained details of: \n• The firm’s international affiliations. \n• Personal achievements and awards of Mr. P as a tax expert. \n• Notable clients handled by the firm. \nLater, another partner, Mr. Q, published a congratulatory advertisement in a \nleading newspaper with his photograph on the occasion of opening a new \nbranch office. \nFurther, M/s BAT & Co. was appointed as the statutory auditor of RST Ltd., a \ncompany covered under CARO 2020. While reporting under Paragraph 3 of \nCARO 2020 relating to property, plant and equipment, inventory, statutory \ndues, and borrowings, the audit team relied on system-generated MIS reports \nfrom the company’s ERP system, and management representations confirming \nthe accuracy and completeness of such information. \nThe audit team did not carry out independent verification of underlying records \nor evaluate the effectiveness of internal controls, on the assumption that \nconsistency between MIS reports and management representations provides \nsufficient audit evidence. \nBased on the above facts, answer the following MCQs:",
